fective <italic>Dictyocaulus </italic>larvae from herbage</article-title><source>Vet Parasitol</source><year>1975</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0304-4017(75)90008-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murrell</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Slotved</surname><given-names>H-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Eriksen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bjerregaard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nansen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Roepstorff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improved method for the recovery of Ascaris suum larvae from pig intestinal mucosa</article-title><source>J Parasitol</source><year>1997</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>321</fpage><lpage>324</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9105321</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3284466</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mwegoha</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>J&#x000f8;rgensen</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Recovery of infective 3rd stage larvae of <italic>Haemonchus contortus </italic>and Ostertagia ostertagi by migration in agar gel</article-title><source>Acta Vet Scand</source><year>1977</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>293</fpage><lpage>299</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">910655</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oksanen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Eriksen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Roepstorff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ils&#x000f8;</surname><given-nam